{"uid":"54121ed4f83d0571","name":"test_timeline_row_opens_the_iteration_dialog","fullName":"tests.test_browser_hub#test_timeline_row_opens_the_iteration_dialog","historyId":"59b8eafea826ec13c932a00ec8e858e0","time":{"start":1791867535564,"stop":1791867569538,"duration":33974},"description":"Task 020 (#18.1, restructured into labelled regions by #81): clicking a\n    timeline row opens THAT iteration's own story as three distinctly\n    LABELLED regions matching the on-disk layout -- outcome (`meta.json`)\n    FIRST, then input (`prompt.md`), then logs (`output.jsonl`) -- so an\n    iteration that ended with a non-zero exit is readable without scrolling\n    past the transcript.\n\n    Everything asserted here is a string Python formatted (`ui_server.\n    iteration_view` -> `state.iteration_summary_lines`/`read_iteration_prompt`\n    + the shared `log_render`), so the hub cannot word an exit reason or a\n    cost differently from `ralphctl iteration`; the fixture has no container\n    at all, since the endpoint is on-disk by design. Also pins the rendering\n    discipline (a transcript containing markup stays TEXT) and that the\n    dialog does not stack across the 4s `load()` rebuild behind it.\n    ","descriptionHtml":"<p>Task 020 (#18.1, restructured into labelled regions by #81): clicking a<br />\ntimeline row opens THAT iteration's own story as three distinctly<br />\nLABELLED regions matching the on-disk layout -- outcome (<code>meta.json</code>)<br />\nFIRST, then input (<code>prompt.md</code>), then logs (<code>output.jsonl</code>) -- so an<br />\niteration that ended with a non-zero exit is readable without scrolling<br />\npast the transcript.</p>\n<pre><code>Everything asserted here is a string Python formatted (`ui_server.\niteration_view` -&gt; `state.iteration_summary_lines`/`read_iteration_prompt`\n+ the shared `log_render`), so the hub cannot word an exit reason or a\ncost differently from `ralphctl iteration`; the fixture has no container\nat all, s